{
  "id": "COMPOUND:20134 - PROTEIN:5811",
  "verbalization": "Marsdekoiside A is shown to interact with VMRC-LCP through multiple indirect pathways, with the most direct route involving the enzyme Carboxylesterase 2. This enzyme is targeted by Marsdekoiside A, and its downstream target, (1S,3R,6S,8R,11S,12S,15R,16R)-15-[(2R)-4-[(2R)-3,3-dimethyloxiran-2-yl]butan-2-yl]-7,7,12,16-tetramethylpentacyclo[9.7.0.01,3.03,8.012,16]octadecan-6-ol, which in turn targets VMRC-LCP. The second pathway involves Marsdekoiside A interacting with HuT78, which is targeted by Methylseleno carboxyethylglutamine, another enzyme that ultimately affects VMRC-LCP. The third pathway links Marsdekoiside A to NCI-H446, which also targets VMRC-LCP. These findings suggest that Marsdekoiside A may exert its effects through a series of enzymatic interactions that ultimately modulate VMRC-LCP. The evidence supports a mechanistic link between Marsdekoiside A and VMRC-LCP, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
